217 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H3
/T (A Heterogeneous Condition While autism has a strong genetic basis, the specific genetic factors vary widely, with hundreds of genes and mutations contributing differently to its manifestation. This variability extends to traits, intensity, associated conditions, and underlying biological mechanisms. For example, autism can coexist with learning disabilities, but most autistic individuals possess average or above-average intelligence, often referred to as 'high-functioning autism.')
/E (A Heterogeneous Condition While autism has a strong genetic basis, the specific genetic factors vary widely, with hundreds of genes and mutations contributing differently to its manifestation. This variability extends to traits, intensity, associated conditions, and underlying biological mechanisms. For example, autism can coexist with learning disabilities, but most autistic individuals possess average or above-average intelligence, often referred to as 'high-functioning autism.')
/Alt ()
/Pg 9 0 R
/K [4]
>>
endobj
